# Lightweight Screen Recorder & Screenshot Tool

A minimalist, floating desktop toolbar for instant screen recording and screenshots. Built with Python, `mss`, OpenCV, and Tkinter.

---

# Why Choose This Over OBS or Other Recorders?

| Feature            | Lightweight Screen Recorder                                                          | OBS Studio / Standard Recorders |
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
| **Resource Usage** | Extremely low CPU/RAM (~12 FPS default, no GPU canvas rendering)                      | Heavy background CPU/GPU usage |
| **User Interface** | Minimal 3-button floating overlay bar (⏺ 📷 ⋮)                                       | Complex multi-pane UI with scenes/sources |
| **Workflow**       | Instant 1-click recording & auto-saves to disk with zero prompts                      | Requires configuring sources, scenes, and output paths |
| **Portability**    | Standalone `.exe` / `.app` that can be pinned to taskbar or desktop                   | Full installer suite with system drivers |
| **Screenshots**    | Native 1-click full-screen capture auto-hiding the UI                                 | Requires hotkey setup or third-party tool |

============================================================================================================================================================

# Features

- Minimalist Overlay: Compact, dark-mode 3-button toolbar (Record, Screenshot, Settings).
- Draggable UI: Position the toolbar anywhere on your screen.
- Zero-Prompt Auto-Save: Files automatically save to `~/Videos/ScreenCapture` with timestamped filenames.
- Smart Screenshotting: UI automatically hides for a fraction of a second when taking a screenshot so it doesn't appear in the capture.
- Persistent Settings: Remembers your chosen save folder across app restarts.

---

# Installation & Setup

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
